window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-55a75b0a2d99cdd4"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"build-a-launch-campaign-kit\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">编制发布活动资料包</h1> <p>将发布背景整理为彼此协调的初稿活动材料。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供发布计划、产品笔记、跟踪表、页面链接、团队讨论、创意素材和审批要求，然后请它起草一套活动资料包，并标记未经核实的主张和待解决的发布问题。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要准备多份配套初稿材料的产品或营销发布活动。</li> <li>涉及发布计划、页面链接、创意简报、跟踪表和团队讨论的团队。</li> <li>需要明确审查主张、审批项和内部运营细节的活动。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>收集已批准的发布计划、产品笔记、简报和模板。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取发布决策、团队背景信息和待解决的问题。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/gmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">gmail（需联网）</a></td> <td>查看相关的发布邮件讨论串和审批信息。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>以结构化资料包的形式起草简报、文案、计划和审批说明。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$slides</code></td> <td>如果活动需要演示文稿，则创建或更新可编辑的发布演示文稿。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>编制发布活动资料包</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请为 [product or launch] 编制一份发布活动资料包初稿。\n\n使用发布计划、产品笔记、发布跟踪表、创意简报、页面链接、团队讨论、审批要求以及我提供的其他来源。\n\n请返回：\n- 发布审查简报\n- 客户邮件\n- 内部公告\n- 社交媒体帖子\n- 两周内容计划\n- 代理机构或创意简报\n- 预发布页面问题清单\n- 团队状态更新\n\n标出未经核实的主张、缺失素材、待审批事项，以及需要产品或法务审查的内容。不要发布或发送任何内容。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/how-to-use-codex-for-everyday-work/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy：日常工作（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"gather-the-launch-record\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">汇总发布记录</h2> <p>活动需要协调发布计划、产品笔记、跟踪表、页面、创意素材和团队决策。请从已批准的来源集合开始，并告诉 ChatGPT 哪些主张、素材和目标页面仍需审查。</p> <ol> <li>附上发布计划、产品笔记、跟踪表、创意简报和相关页面。</li> <li>补充发布讨论、审批要求、目标受众、时间安排和输出格式。</li> <li>运行起始提示词，创建活动资料包和审批检查清单。</li> <li>根据产品来源核实主张，并将公开文案与内部运营内容分开。</li> <li>渲染任何演示文稿或页面草稿，并在交由人工审查前修复安全范围内的版式问题。</li> </ol> <p>首次生成的内容应先用于找出缺失输入，不要用看似合理的文案填补空缺。法律、产品和品牌审查标记应放在其所涉及的材料旁边。</p> <p><a id=\"run-a-launch-readiness-pass\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">检查发布准备情况</h2> <p>请 ChatGPT 根据发布计划检查资料包，只列出可能阻碍审查或发布的差距。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Audit this campaign kit against the launch plan and approval guidance.\n\nList:\n\n- claims without a source\n- assets or links that are missing\n- inconsistent dates, names, or product descriptions\n- items needing product, legal, brand, or owner approval\n- staging-page issues\n- public copy that includes internal-only details\n\nFix safe formatting issues, but do not publish, send, or approve anything.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请对照发布计划和审批要求，审查这套营销活动材料。\n\n列出：\n\n- 没有来源支持的主张\n- 缺失的素材或链接\n- 不一致的日期、名称或产品描述\n- 需要产品、法务、品牌或负责人批准的事项\n- 预发布页面存在的问题\n- 包含仅限内部使用细节的公开文案\n\n修复可以安全处理的格式问题，但不要发布、发送或批准任何内容。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-a-launch-campaign-kit\">Build a launch campaign kit</h1> <p>Turn launch context into coordinated first-draft campaign assets.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT launch plans, product notes, trackers, page links, team discussion, creative inputs, and approval guidance, then ask it to draft a campaign kit with review flags for unverified claims and staging issues.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Product or marketing launches that need several coordinated first-draft assets.</li> <li>Teams working across launch plans, page links, creative briefs, trackers, and discussion threads.</li> <li>Campaigns where claims, approvals, and private operational details need explicit review.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Gather approved launch plans, product notes, briefs, and templates.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Read launch decisions, team context, and open questions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/gmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">gmail (online)</a></td> <td>Check relevant launch email threads and approvals.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Draft the brief, copy, plan, and approval notes in a structured package.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$slides</code></td> <td>Create or update an editable launch presentation when the campaign needs a deck.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build the launch campaign kit</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Build a first-draft campaign kit for [product or launch].\n\nUse the launch plan, product notes, launch tracker, creative brief, page links, team discussions, approval guidance, and any other sources I provide.\n\nReturn:\n- launch review brief\n- customer email\n- internal announcement\n- social post\n- two-week content plan\n- agency or creative brief\n- staging-page fix list\n- team status update\n\nFlag unverified claims, missing assets, approval needs, and anything that requires product or legal review. Do not publish or send anything.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/how-to-use-codex-for-everyday-work/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy: Everyday work (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"gather-the-launch-record\">Gather the launch record</h2> <p>Campaign work crosses plans, product notes, trackers, pages, creative inputs, and team decisions. Start with the approved source set and tell ChatGPT which claims, assets, and destinations still need review.</p> <ol> <li>Attach the launch plan, product notes, tracker, creative brief, and relevant pages.</li> <li>Add launch discussions, approval guidance, audience, timing, and destination formats.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt to create the campaign kit and an approval checklist.</li> <li>Verify claims against product sources and separate public copy from internal operations.</li> <li>Render any deck or page draft and fix safe layout issues before human review.</li> </ol> <p>Use the first pass to identify missing inputs, not to fill them with plausible copy. Keep legal, product, and brand review flags next to the asset they affect.</p> <h2 id=\"run-a-launch-readiness-pass\">Run a launch-readiness pass</h2> <p>Ask ChatGPT to compare the kit with the launch plan and return only the gaps that could block review or publication.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Audit this campaign kit against the launch plan and approval guidance.\n\nList:\n\n- claims without a source\n- assets or links that are missing\n- inconsistent dates, names, or product descriptions\n- items needing product, legal, brand, or owner approval\n- staging-page issues\n- public copy that includes internal-only details\n\nFix safe formatting issues, but do not publish, send, or approve anything.\n</code></pre>"};
